uccess","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Before concluding arbitrage has failed, the board should first test measurement artifacts:**\n\n- **Timing:** Does the NAV strike align with the official closing auction? Check for stale or fair-valued prices, late corporate actions, and the treatment of accruals and cash.\n- **Peers:** Do similar ETFs and index futures show the same pattern? If so, the cause is likely market-wide (sector stress, factor dislocation).\n- **Underlying frictions:** Look at illiquid, small-cap or hard-to-borrow constituents, wide spreads, short-sale constraints, and settlement or creation-basket mismatches.\n- **AP and market-maker participation:** Review how many APs are active, their creation/redemption volumes, any fee or cutoff changes, balance-sheet constraints, and lead market maker quoting quality.\n\n**Inquiry:** Ask the adviser for a documented analysis covering intraday iNAV versus price, basket data and AP interviews.\n\n**Corrective options:**\n- Adjust custom baskets or cash-in-lieu rules.\n- Revise transaction fees.\n- Recruit more APs or market makers.\n- Refine fair-value procedures.\n- Enhance disclosure. Under Rule 6c-11, a premium or discount above 2% for more than seven consecutive days requires a website explanation, not automatic remediation.","ttft_ms":2229,"type":"result","duration_ms":6322,"uuid":"6e19df91-7896-4eef-805a-5770fda000e2","ttft_stream_ms":1064,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":1064,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
